        ;; main, and the reason it was not main is gone.
        ;;
        ;; This pinned a hotfix branch because main had moved the state
        ;; encoding three times (a governance leaf, `:deficit`, pending
        ;; withdrawals) and I had concluded that advancing to it forks the
        ;; chain: replicas on either side compute different state roots for
        ;; identical state, which is the shape of the divergence the root
        ;; exists to catch.
        ;;
        ;; **That conclusion was wrong.** A block is
        ;; `height / parent-hash / proposals / proposer / ts`
        ;; (`inga.consensus/canonical-block`) and nothing else. It carries no
        ;; state root, `inga.consensus` never mentions one, and
        ;; `inga.replica/state-root` is computed on demand from machine state
        ;; for REPORTING. Consensus orders transactions; it never compares
        ;; what executing them produced.
        ;;
        ;; So an encoding change is an ordinary deploy. Replicas report
        ;; different roots while the rollout is in flight — the window is real
        ;; and visible in `/head` — and converge once all four run the same
        ;; code, which is exactly what was observed when a divergent replica
        ;; restarted onto unified code and replayed.
        ;;
        ;; What this brings live: collateral totals under the root
        ;; (`commit/reserves`), bad debt as `:deficit` rather than a negative
        ;; balance, withdrawals that raise a claim instead of deleting money,
        ;; who may mint committed to the root, liquidation driven by the block
        ;; rather than by a keeper, and cancel-all / amend.
        io.github.kotoba-lang/torihiki
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/torihiki.git"
         :git/sha "96f6daf909bd42ecf2045b97192b96f10aef670f"}
